      <p begin="01:09:58.875" end="01:09:59.833">change their APIs.</p>
      <p begin="01:10:00.208" end="01:10:01.500">You need coverage pattern shift,</p>
      <p begin="01:10:02.083" end="01:10:03.958">user behaviors evolved, and category</p>
      <p begin="01:10:03.958" end="01:10:05.708">definitions drift. This</p>
      <p begin="01:10:05.750" end="01:10:07.500">creates conceptual drift and data</p>
      <p begin="01:10:07.500" end="01:10:10.416">drift. So concept drift is the</p>
      <p begin="01:10:10.416" end="01:10:11.333">meaning of the category</p>
      <p begin="01:10:11.333" end="01:10:13.250">changes. Data drift is the</p>
      <p begin="01:10:13.250" end="01:10:15.500">distinction of the data changes. And</p>
      <p begin="01:10:15.500" end="01:10:17.250">then we have static validation as</p>
      <p begin="01:10:17.250" end="01:10:19.666">inadequate. So if your data set</p>
      <p begin="01:10:19.666" end="01:10:21.541">spans years, you might monitor</p>
      <p begin="01:10:21.541" end="01:10:22.833">stability for this case.</p>
      <p begin="01:10:28.708" end="01:10:29.625">So one thing to remember, the</p>
      <p begin="01:10:29.625" end="01:10:31.333">documentation is not weakness. It's</p>
      <p begin="01:10:31.333" end="01:10:32.375">a methodological clarity.</p>
      <p begin="01:10:32.875" end="01:10:34.583">You should explicitly state known</p>
      <p begin="01:10:34.583" end="01:10:36.666">biases, blind spots, assumptions</p>
      <p begin="01:10:36.666" end="01:10:37.875">required for inference,</p>
      <p begin="01:10:38.541" end="01:10:39.958">data generation constraints.</p>
      <p begin="01:10:40.958" end="01:10:41.791">Transparenting is going to</p>
      <p begin="01:10:41.791" end="01:10:42.791">strengthen your credibility.</p>
      <p begin="01:10:43.291" end="01:10:44.958">Reviewers are more skeptical when</p>
      <p begin="01:10:44.958" end="01:10:46.125">limitations are hidden.</p>
      <p begin="01:10:50.708" end="01:10:52.291">So one thing is that data quality is</p>
      <p begin="01:10:52.291" end="01:10:53.958">not a cleanup choice.</p>
      <p begin="01:10:54.166" end="01:10:55.208">It's a design principle.</p>
      <p begin="01:10:56.208" end="01:10:58.208">It should be anticipated collection,</p>
      <p begin="01:10:58.666" end="01:10:59.875">monitored over time,</p>
      <p begin="01:11:00.458" end="01:11:02.208">quantified where possible, and</p>
      <p begin="01:11:02.208" end="01:11:03.500">reported alongside results.</p>
      <p begin="01:11:04.333" end="01:11:05.750">Validation is part of methodology.</p>
      <p begin="01:11:06.750" end="01:11:08.291">You need to justify your</p>
      <p begin="01:11:08.291" end="01:11:08.875">identification</p>
      <p begin="01:11:08.875" end="01:11:11.208">assumptions, and you must justify</p>
      <p begin="01:11:11.500" end="01:11:17.250">measurement assumptions for it. So</p>
      <p begin="01:11:17.250" end="01:11:18.791">for guiding principles for you, you</p>
      <p begin="01:11:18.791" end="01:11:19.583">want to treat biases</p>
      <p begin="01:11:19.958" end="01:11:22.458">as a structural. You want to</p>
      <p begin="01:11:22.458" end="01:11:25.666">validate at multiple stages. You</p>
      <p begin="01:11:25.666" end="01:11:27.708">want to separate reliability from</p>
      <p begin="01:11:27.750" end="01:11:30.166">validity. You want to document</p>
      <p begin="01:11:30.166" end="01:11:32.708">uncertainty explicitly. So these</p>
      <p begin="01:11:32.708" end="01:11:33.416">principles are going to</p>
      <p begin="01:11:33.416" end="01:11:34.625">apply to a variety of data</p>
      <p begin="01:11:34.625" end="01:11:38.125">collection processes like API data,</p>
      <p begin="01:11:38.666" end="01:11:41.291">LLM generated data, hand-coded data,</p>
      <p begin="01:11:41.833" end="01:11:43.333">remote sensing data, survey data,</p>
      <p begin="01:11:43.750" end="01:11:44.583">much of what we're</p>
      <p begin="01:11:44.583" end="01:11:45.500">covering in the course.</p>
      <p begin="01:11:46.291" end="01:11:47.375">But measurement is going</p>
      <p begin="01:11:47.375" end="01:11:48.416">to precede your modeling.</p>
      <p begin="01:11:51.625" end="01:11:53.000">So just a couple of things to keep</p>
      <p begin="01:11:53.000" end="01:11:55.500">in mind for it with these three</p>
      <p begin="01:11:55.500" end="01:11:56.833">questions. So which biases</p>
      <p begin="01:11:57.041" end="01:11:58.500">are hardest to detect when you're</p>
      <p begin="01:11:58.500" end="01:12:01.125">starting a research project? Often</p>
      <p begin="01:12:01.125" end="01:12:02.541">the hardest bias is those</p>
      <p begin="01:12:02.541" end="01:12:03.541">that are aligned with our</p>
      <p begin="01:12:03.541" end="01:12:04.458">expectations. So when is validation</p>
      <p begin="01:12:04.458" end="01:12:06.375">expectations. So when is validation</p>
      <p begin="01:12:06.375" end="01:12:07.750">infeasible? So often the hardest,</p>
      <p begin="01:12:07.750" end="01:12:09.208">when is validation infeasible? So</p>
      <p begin="01:12:09.208" end="01:12:11.916">maybe when no ground truth exists.</p>
      <p begin="01:12:13.458" end="01:12:15.916">And then how should uncertainty</p>
